# `@: Model m make 3`: a candidate whose first item names a callable is that call (book section 9), one value, and
# the call keeps its own reason -- the call check reads `make` with no actuals and refuses its arity, as for `r:
# twice 3` -- not the declaration's (DECLARATION-CANDIDATE-ROLE).
Model:
    int: value 7
end: Model
fn: make (int: k) @: Model
    return: @ Model
end: make
fn: check () int
    @: Model m make 3
    return: 7
end: check
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
